data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":3933,"item_id":"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae4a234abf88191a7cd83d7441a2dff","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"candidate\":8,\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"original_context_note\":\"Compared spec.full_target literally with target-selection.json/full_target and mathematically with problem.md:14-30. The nonempty compact E, every ambient dimension n≥0 including zero, closed interval [0,1], Euclidean metric, unnormalized diameter costs and empty-set dimension convention are preserved. H001 is the disclosed original nonemptiness assumption; H002 is compactness. H003 explicitly retains the original n≥0 range and is unused because n is represented by its equivalent natural-number dimension type; no negative dimension is selected or excluded beyond the original range. No original assumption has been deleted, and no proof claim is an H. The original route is R001's bounded-box estimate, R002's positive-diameter covers and vertical interval subdivision, R003's arbitrary-cover projections/open interval enlargements and nonnegative integration, R004's s↑D argument, and R005's interval-length estimate and isometric vertical copy, followed by R006. No material calculation or required limiting argument from problem.md:49-167 has been omitted. Definitions D001-D008 give the Euclidean coordinate metric, extended diameter, the original positive-scale/exponent content and supremum formulas, dimension, I,F,D and Lebesgue conventions. They are total on their declared domains and require no unproved project guards. In particular D007 does NOT assume finite dimension: R001 proves it before it is used as a real. The definition of compactness in D001 is unfolded to get finite ball subcovers in R001, not treated as an imported compactness theorem. All selected non-H vertices are in P's AND closure, every N/P has its displayed unique producer, and H003 is the only unused H. Source checks: successful native probes M001-M006, their whole signatures and axioms, and source readbacks at Lebesgue/Add:360-372, Lebesgue/Basic:84-85 and 527-529, OuterMeasure/Basic:44-72, and Lebesgue-measure/Basic:48-96 match the full project statements, including countability, AEMeasurability and OuterMeasureClass premises. Only ordinary classical/propositional/extensional axioms occur in the probe reports. E001 remains explicitly UNVERIFIED_PRIMARY: ordered arxiv, Google text, Google DOI and confirmed-DOI Sci-Hub/browser attempts failed, and defer_primary_source bound the exact complete problem.md:34-47 quotation. Its edition, original theorem locator, standing context and errata have NOT been verified. Thus my closing mathematical inspection is conditional on the displayed E001 statement; it is not a source-fidelity PASS, ordinary Audit A or an unconditional theorem certification. The deferred source record and warning must remain in delivery.\",\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions N001 against R001/S001-S004. It exports boundedness, finite content at EVERY s>0 and δ>0, nonnegative finite D≤n, and the n=0 singleton assertion. F001 supplies the first two, F002 the positive-n bound via arbitrarily fine grid covers, and F003 the singleton and D=0 case. These are exactly the facts R002, R003, R004 and R006 consume; no downstream node needs an unexported chosen box or finite cover.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"R002/S001 proves the zero-ambient branch using actual isometric interval-cover inverse images. S002-S004 give covers with scale sqrt(2)r and exact cost factor 2(sqrt(2))^(q+1)ε; S005 makes every fixed-scale content zero. S006 closes q>D and n≥1 and passes q↓D using N001 finiteness. Thus the exported inequality and finiteness clause are both proved, with no hidden n≥1 assumption in N002.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"R003/S001-S005 establishes the exported content inequality for all positive s and δ, not merely for s<D or a special cover. The error bound is uniform after removing the auxiliary J,η,ε: S004 proves every arbitrary δ-cover of F has cost≥c; S005 takes its infimum. No arbitrary-cover measurability assumption, chosen interval sequence or equation-number reference is needed by R004.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"Checked R004/S001-S002 proves precisely D>0⇒dim_H F≥D+1. The implication retains its antecedent after discharging L1. For every 0<s<D, E001 and the full N003 scale inequality give infinite (s+1)-measure, then dimension≥s+1; N001 finiteness permits s↑D. There is no claim of a lower bound from a nonexistent s when D=0.\"},{\"id\":\"N005\",\"note\":\"R005/S001-S004 proves both bounds on dim_H I, including the quantitative lower content δ^(s-1) at every δ>0 and 0<s<1, handling zero diameters separately. F004 exports infinite interval measures within this same R. S005 uses H001 for x0 and explicitly pulls arbitrary F covers back along the vertical isometry. It proves dim_H F≥1 for all n, whence the stated D=0 consequence. The exported statement does not require consumers to know x0 or the private pullback family.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"R006/S001 uses only the exported N001,N002,N004,N005. Nonnegative finite D is either positive or zero; the respective complete lower-bound interfaces and the unconditional upper bound give equality. Substituting D007 and D006 yields exactly spec.conclusion and the complete selected theorem, on the stipulated Euclidean coordinate-adjoining space, including n=0.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual conditional packet (unchanged read retained from candidate 7). H002 and D001's compactness definition yield finite ball subcovers in S001; this gives finite scale contents directly, and a finite coordinate maximum gives the box witness in F001. H001 supplies the singleton conclusion in S003 and excludes an empty E. S002 counts ceil(2B/h)^n cubes, bounds each diameter by sqrt(n)h, and bounds cost by C n^(s/2)h^(s-n) with C=(2B+1)^n independent of h. With s>n the cost tends to zero while scale tends to zero, so the use of zero measure is warranted. S003 separately treats n=0 at all positive exponents. L1,L2 are discharged and the natural-number cases are exhaustive in S004. Real-power limits, finite maxima and elementary infimum consequences here are routine standard steps with their positivity and boundedness conditions displayed, not additional core dimension results.\",\"source_application_check\":\"R001/A001 sets E001's A=E and exponent s>n>0, after S002 constructs arbitrarily small-cost covers at every target scale. Its delivered D≤s entails D≤n by the closed order bound. A002 sets A=E⊆Eucl(0) and each s>0, after the singleton cover gives zero s-measure. No source claim about product dimension is used. E001 is a conditional direct input with exactly the displayed diameter normalization; its unverified primary status is separately preserved.\",\"declaration_check\":\"B is a witness chosen at S002 from the EARLIER existence F001, not from a declared property without proof. C,h,s have their displayed definitions/positive ranges within the n>0 grid calculation; C depends only on B,n, not on h. Quantified exponents and scales in S001 and S003 are sentence-bound and close there. All global objects are D001-D004,D007 and the two parameters; F002/F003 export no private grid witness. D remains extended nonnegative until the proved finite bound permits a real interpretation.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the current candidate-8 packet. N001 alone provides the n=0 singleton, D=0, and D≥0/finiteness needed here; no compactness or nonemptiness is imported from its producer. S002 uses the direct E001 zero-measure clause, then the defining infimum supplies the small-cost cover; singleton replacement has strictly positive diameters only in the n≥1 branch, with added cost≤ε/2. S003 gives 1/N_i≤r_i and N_i≤2/r_i using 0<r_i≤1. The Euclidean product diameter is bounded by sqrt(2)r_i, and S004 retains the exact cost factor. S005 uses F003 at min(1,δ/sqrt(2)) and arbitrary tolerance, not the expired private r,ε. S006 closes L3 and L2 and the q↓D argument; S001 closed L1. All inputs have actual roles, and all local assumptions remain antecedents until properly discharged.\",\"source_application_check\":\"A001 uses E001 with F⊆Eucl(1), a>1 after equal subdivision covers prove H^a(F)=0. A002 uses A=E, q>D, with q>0 obtained from N001, giving H^q(E)=0. A003 uses A=F⊆Eucl(n+1), exponent q+1>0 after S005 proves H^(q+1)(F)=0 at every scale. The Euclidean metric is unchanged in each instance; there is no isometry-invariance theorem silently replacing the cover argument in the n=0 branch.\",\"declaration_check\":\"a is scoped to S001. q spans the positive-dimensional branch and is universally closed before q↓D. r,ε are arbitrary only for S002-S004. U is chosen at S003 from earlier F002; r_i and N_i are then explicitly defined from U. Indices i and j are bound by their displayed countable and finite ranges. Their finite-product family is countable and its private identity does not escape F003. F003 uses fresh statement binders r0,ε0; δ is newly arbitrary at S005. Output contains only the global F,D,dim_H.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the unchanged packet retained from candidate 7. The only project fact used from N001 is c=H^s_δ(E)<∞; the producer's compactness argument is not imported. Under L1 and L2 the distance formula bounds both projection diameters by ρ_i≤δ. S001 constructs the actual open enlargement using inf/sup of each nonempty bounded B_i and η_i>0, proving existence before choosing J. S002 derives the pointwise slice-cover inequality directly from membership in arbitrary V_i. S003 integrates constant indicators on the whole real line, making both sides zero off I. Every integrand is nonnegative Borel, so the nonnegative interchange is legitimate even if the cost series is infinite. The error is bounded by ε sum_i2^(-i-1)=ε; ρ_i=0 causes no division or negative power. S004 separately handles infinite and finite cost, removes ε while V,c,ρ stay fixed, then removes the arbitrary cover. S005 infimizes costs and closes s,δ. No measurability of V_i,A_i,B_i, finite total cost, or signed-integral exchange is assumed.\",\"source_application_check\":\"At S003, M002 is instantiated with f=c1_I and g=sum_iρ_i^s1_(J_i∩I); F002 establishes the pointwise inequality on I and both sides vanish outside it. M001 has X=R Borel, μ=λ, K=N, source family g_i; J_i open-or-empty and I closed make each constant indicator Borel and hence AEMeasurable. M003/A101 evaluates f using Borel I; A102 evaluates each g_i using Borel J_i∩I, with constants c and ρ_i^s nonnegative finite. M005 uses endpoints 0,1. M006 uses the endpoints of the CHOSEN J_i, and F001 bounds their length by ρ_i+η_i; empty J_i are handled separately. These native results deliver exactly the displayed c≤sum_iρ_i^sλ(J_i∩I), followed by the stated length/error estimates. Basic measure monotonicity and Borel closure are routine standard facts with the actual containments and measurable sets displayed.\",\"declaration_check\":\"s,δ,V,ε are arbitrary and positivity/cover properties are temporary L1,L2,L3, not new roots. ρ,A,B,η are defined by actual formulas from V,s,ε. c's finite-real interpretation is justified by direct N001 under L1. The family J is a witness from the earlier F001 and lasts through integration; f,g are then explicitly defined. Scalar t and x in the slice argument and summation indices are bound where used. After closing ε and V, F004 and the final output contain none of the private enlargement data. All source functions and measures have the required domains/codomains; no restricted-measure identification is left unstated.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read candidate 8. Only N001,N003,E001 are used. Under L1 D>0 and L2 0<s<D, the E001 infinite-measure clause and the complete scale comparison N003 imply H^(s+1)(F)=∞ by suprema. The additional small-scale monotonicity assertion is justified by inclusion of admissible cover classes, not assumed. Infinite measure then yields the bound dim_H F≥s+1; L2 is discharged into the quantified F001. S002 uses N001 finiteness and explicit exponents D-D/k with k>1 to approach D, without redefining the earlier arbitrary s. L1 is discharged to export the implication. There is no use of R003's private c or intervals.\",\"source_application_check\":\"A001 sets E001's A=E, exponent s with 0<s<D=dim_H E, exactly L2. A002 sets A=F and exponent s+1>0; the infinite measure premise is the preceding supremum comparison using N003 at each δ>0. These applications require no compactness beyond the finite D supplied by N001 and no normalization bridge, since both input statements use D003.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The arbitrary s exists only in S001. L1 persists to S002 but L2 does not. F001 has its own bound real variable v and exports the whole interval of lower bounds. In S002 v is bound in the supremum description and k is the explicitly integer-indexed approach sequence. No chosen exponent or small scale escapes, and the output has only the global D,F,dim_H.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the current candidate-8 packet. S001's equal interval covers establish the upper bound independently of N002 or its producer. Under L1-L3, S002 constructs the open interval enlargements from bounded nonempty W_i; S003 applies length subadditivity only to the J_i, gets 1≤sumρ_i+ε, removes ε and derives sumρ_i≥1. The estimate ρ_i^s≥δ^(s-1)ρ_i explicitly separates ρ_i=0 and uses s-1<0 only for positive ρ_i. Infimum and δ↓0 in S004 give H^s(I)=∞, and F004 includes this full quantified fact. In S005 H001 genuinely supplies x0; the vertical map's Euclidean distance identity proves the actual pullback diameter bound. Temporary L4 is discharged before infimizing over covers and taking suprema, so the final comparison holds for every positive exponent and scale. F004 and the direct E001 then give dim_H F≥1; D=0 and n=0 are retained. No general dimension monotonicity/isometry theorem or other producer body is imported.\",\"source_application_check\":\"At S003, M004 has the measure type on the Borel real line as G, λ as μ, N as countable index, and J_i as the sets; the FunLike/OuterMeasureClass structures are those of this measure, and no W_i measurability is required. M005 uses endpoints 0,1. M006 uses the endpoints of each bounded chosen J_i, with F002 giving the length bound. E001/A001 applies at a>1 after zero interval measure is proved; A002 applies at 0<s<1 after the content lower bounds force infinity. A003 applies to F with every 0<v<1 after the fully displayed isometric pullback comparison and F004 force H^v(F)=∞. The positivity and Euclidean-set conditions are explicit in each instance.\",\"declaration_check\":\"a is local to the upper bound; s,δ live only through S004, and W,ρ,ε,J only in the interval-cover portion. J is chosen from an earlier proved F002, not postulated as measurable. The arbitrary source exponent and scale v,d and the arbitrary F-cover V are separately declared at S005, with their range/cover assumptions recorded in L4. x0 is chosen from H001 and T_i is explicitly defined from x0,V,I. Bound t,u,i occur only within the stated maps, sets and distance formulas. All private variables are removed from the final dimension assertions; no expired δ or s from the first portion is used as a free datum in S005.\"},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the unchanged retained packet from candidate 7, which contains exactly N001,N002,N004,N005. N001 gives finite nonnegative D, N004 supplies the positive case, N005 the zero case, and N002 the common finite upper bound. Exhaustiveness follows from D≥0. Order antisymmetry and substitution of the supplied definitions prove the exact output; no extra H, E, ancestor body or interval-measure fact is used.\",\"source_application_check\":\"There is no direct E/M application in R006. Each N input is used solely for a clause explicitly in its exported statement: N001 for D≥0 and finiteness, N002 for the upper bound, N004 for its D>0 implication, N005 for dim_H F≥1 when D=0. Definitions D006,D007 identify this equality with the desired product formula; D001 fixes the Euclidean metric.\",\"declaration_check\":\"There are no private witnesses or free locals. All occurring objects are n,E and the defined Eucl,I,F,D,dim_H. The positive/zero cases introduce no escaping data. The concluding substitution uses the original coordinate-adjoining identification rather than a different product norm.\"}] }"}

